From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 18:41:17 +0000
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: fix the FRITZ!Box 7560 LED polarity and labels

The board's six LEDs were transcribed from AVM's 4.9 board description,
arch/mips/boot/dts/lantiq/avm/grx350_common.dtsi, active levels and node
names included. A panel test on real hardware says two of those fields
were wrong at the source, and it is not hard to see why nobody noticed:
AVM does not drive these lines through gpio-leds. Each one is exported
individually by the out-of-tree "avm,avm_gpio_generic" shim, which takes
the bank and pin out of the node and then writes the raw level itself.
The active-level flag is never consulted and the node name is never
matched against anything, so both fields were decorative in the vendor
tree and were free to drift away from the board without anything ever
complaining.

Polarity. Driving a line high with its pad muxed to GPIO turns the
corresponding LED off, and driving it low turns it on -- the opposite of
what the transcribed GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH says. Four of the six were watched
going dark by eye as their line was driven high, and the bank's output
register was read back on each step so that an unlit LED could not be
confused with a write that never reached the pad. The panel LEDs hang
off 3V3 with the SoC pin as the sink, so all six become
GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW.

Labels. Walking the panel one line at a time also shows two of the names
pointing at the wrong lamp: gpio0 3, which the vendor tree calls
"festnetz", lights the LED silkscreened DECT, and gpio0 18, which it
calls "internet", lights the one silkscreened Fon. A 7560 panel has no
Internet LED at all -- the uplink was DSL and its state shares the Power
LED -- so "green:internet" was naming a lamp that does not exist on this
board. Rename the two to green:dect and green:fon, and rename their
phandle labels to match.

led-boot / led-running / led-failsafe / led-upgrade / led-wifi keep
pointing at the same four LEDs; none of the aliases referenced either
renamed node. The power LED's default-state stays "on": gpio-leds
resolves that through the polarity flag, so "on" still means lit, it
just now drives the pad low to get there.

The buttons and the DECT reset hog are deliberately untouched. The two
buttons really are active low -- they read as released with the line
high and pressed with it pulled down -- and the hog is not a panel line,
so neither is affected by any of the above.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi
index fc303f1393ed..6199a76a1fdf 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi
@@ -83,6 +83,11 @@ reserved-memory {
 };
 
 / {
+	/*
+	 * Every line here is active low: the panel LEDs hang off 3V3 and
+	 * the SoC pin sinks them, so driving the pin high extinguishes
+	 * the LED. Confirmed on hardware, one GPIO at a time.
+	 */
 	leds {
 		compatible = "gpio-leds";
 
@@ -95,38 +100,40 @@ leds {
 		 */
 		led_power: led-0 {
 			label = "green:power";
-			gpios = <&gpio1 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			gpios = <&gpio1 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			default-state = "on";
 		};
 
-		led_internet: led-1 {
-			label = "green:internet";
-			gpios = <&gpio0 18 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		/* Vendor name: gpio_avm_led_internet. Drives "Fon". */
+		led_fon: led-1 {
+			label = "green:fon";
+			gpios = <&gpio0 18 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			default-state = "off";
 		};
 
-		led_festnetz: led-2 {
-			label = "green:festnetz";
-			gpios = <&gpio0 3 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		/* Vendor name: gpio_avm_led_festnetz. Drives "DECT". */
+		led_dect: led-2 {
+			label = "green:dect";
+			gpios = <&gpio0 3 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			default-state = "off";
 		};
 
 		led_wlan: led-3 {
 			label = "green:wlan";
-			gpios = <&gpio0 14 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			gpios = <&gpio0 14 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			default-state = "off";
 		};
 
 		led_info: led-4 {
 			label = "green:info";
-			gpios = <&gpio0 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			gpios = <&gpio0 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			default-state = "off";
 		};
 
 		/* Bank 1, pin 2 == SoC pin 34. */
 		led_info_red: led-5 {
 			label = "red:info";
-			gpios = <&gpio1 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			gpios = <&gpio1 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			default-state = "off";
 		};
 	};
